tatic or recurrent locally advanced Merkel cell carcinoma. The company's clinical stage products include INCB123667 for ovarian cancer; INCB161734 for solid tumors; INCA33890 for cancers; Ruxolitinib cream for atopic dermatitis, hidradenitis suppurativa (HS), and prurigo nodularis; Povorcitinib for HS, nonsegmental vitiligo, prurigo nodularis, and asthma; and INCB00928 for the treatment of fibrodysplasia ossificans progressive. It has collaboration and license agreement with Novartis, Lilly, and Syndax. The company sells its products to specialty and retail pharmacies, hospital pharmacies, and distributors. Incyte Corporation has a clinical trial collaboration with Genmab A/S to evaluate petosemtamab. The company was formerly known as Incyte Genomics Inc and changed its name to Incyte Corporation in March 2003. Incyte Corporation was incorporated in 1991 and is headquartered in Wilmington, Delaware.","employees":2844,"website":"https://www.incyte.com","country":"United States","city":"Wilmington","officers":[{"name":"Mr. William J. Meury","title":"CEO & Director"},{"name":"Dr. Pablo J. Cagnoni M.D., Ph.D.","title":"President and Global Head of R&D"},{"name":"Mr. Thomas  Tray","title":"Principal Financial Officer, VP of Finance & Chief Accounting Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.94,"tpe":30.13,"ps":4.427,"pfcf":28.89,"peg":1.335,"pb":4.543,"ev_ebitda":16.87,"rev_growth":0.102,"eps_growth":0.167,"eps_growth_fwd":0.0901,"eps_growth_next":0.1184,"div_yield":0,"roe":-0.00633,"roa":0.01963,"de":37.14,"gross_margin":0.5204,"op_margin":0.03842,"profit_margin":0,"current_ratio":3.161},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":13.39,"sector":18.94,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":14.85,"sector":30.13,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":4.061,"sector":4.427,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":20.02,"sector":28.89,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":null,"sector":1.3